ndscapers INC employees or agents for the completion of routine governmental administrative actions (so-called facilitation payments), or by any other measure that is unethical or that will tarnish our reputation for honesty and integrity. Even the appearance of such conduct must be avoided.” 4.4 Unethical conduct may or may not constitute illegal or corrupt behaviour. The Landscapers INC Code of Conduct defines ethical behaviour and required standards of conduct. The consequences of violations of the Code by an employee include, but are not limited to, disciplinary action. 4.5 All cases of alleged bribery and corruption will be investigated and followed up by the application of all available remedies. 4.6 Employees who commit an act of bribery or corruption will be subject to disciplinary action, up to and including termination with cause. 5. PROCEDURES FOR PREVENTING BRIBERY AND CORRUPTION The procedures adopted by Landscapers INC to prevent bribery and corruption include applying due diligence procedures and taking a risk-based approach in respect to third parties and associated persons to ensure compliance with all applicable laws and regulations related to anti-bribery and corruption. The procedures applied are proportionate to the related risks and these include but are not limited to, the following: 5.1 A high-level risk assessment is conducted periodically to assess key compliance risks including the risks of bribery and corruption and any other risks in applicable legislation. 5.2 The Landscapers INC Code of Conduct is communicated to all employees. 5.3 Training and communication of policies is comprehensive and ongoing. 5.4 There are divisional initiatives for the implementation of appropriate procedures for preventing and detecting bribery and corruption, including procedures to prevent facilitation procedures. Anti-Bribery and Corruption Policy POL 007 Version: 00 Effective Date: 02-01- 2026 Revision Date: 02-01-2027 5.5 There are approved guidelines in each division on contractual arrangements with third parties in high risk areas and other associated persons, including requirements for them to comply with all applicable laws and regulations related to anti-bribery and corruption. 5.6 There are processes and procedures in place to investigate, respond and report on violations, incidents and other lapses in control. APPROVAL CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.Naidoo 02 January 2026', true, 'manager', 'POL 007', '00', '2026-01-02', '2027-01-02', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/7.Anti-Bribery and Corruption Policy.pdf', true, '{}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, category = excluded.category, content = excluded.content, text = excluded.text, locked = excluded.locked, owner_role = excluded.owner_role, doc_code = excluded.doc_code, revision = excluded.revision, effective_date = excluded.effective_date, review_date = excluded.review_date, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, data = excluded.data where public.docs._seed and public.docs.updated_by is not distinct from public.docs.created_by;
insert into public.docs (id, title, category, content, text, locked, owner_role, doc_code, revision, effective_date, review_date, _src, _seed, data) values ('doc-policy-8-70c882', 'Child Labour Policy', 'policy', '<p>Child Labour Policy PURPOSE Landscapers INC Child Labour Policy has been established in order to make Landscapers INC position clear to suppliers and their co-workers, as well as any other parties. The requirements in this policy are mandatory to all suppliers and their sub-contractors. SCOPE Landscapers INC acknowledges the fact that child labour occurs in many countries. However, Landscapers INC does not accept child labour, and works actively against it. The complexity of the child labour issue requires a consistent, long-term effort to create sustainable and broad- based solutions in order to reach our goal; that no products delivered to Landscapers INC are produced by child labour.</p>
<p>Landscapers INC respects different cultures and values in countries where Landscapers INC operates and sources its products but does not compromise on the basic requirements regarding the Rights of the Child.</p>
<h3>POLICY STATEMENT</h3>
<p>Landscapers INC may not require or permit a child to work if the child is under 15 years of age or is under the minimum school leaving age in terms of the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997. Landscapers INC may also not require or permit a child to perform such work or services that are inappropriate for his/her age; that places a risk to the child’s well-being, education, physical or mental health or social development.</p>
<p>Implementation All actions to avoid child labour shall be implemented by taking the child’s best interests into account. Landscapers INC requires that all suppliers shall recognise the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997, chapter 6, “Prohibition of employment of children and forced labour”. This is regarded as a criminal offence as per the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997, Chapter 6. Suppliers are obliged to take the appropriate measures to ensure that no child labour occurs at suppliers’ and their sub-contractor’s places of production. If child labour is found in any place of production Landscapers INC will require the supplier to implement a corrective action plan. If corrective action is not implemented within the agreed time-frame, or if repeated violations occur Landscapers INC will terminate all business with the supplier concerned. The corrective action plan shall take the child’s best interests into consideration, i.e. family and social situation and level of education. Care shall be taken not merely to move child labour from one supplier’s workplace to another, but to enable more viable and sustainable alternatives for the child’s development.</p>
<p>The supplier shall effectively communicate to all its sub-contractors, as well as to its own co- workers, the content of Landscapers INC Child Labour Policy, and ensure that all measures required are implemented accordingly.</p>
<p>Young Workers Landscapers INC supports the legal employment of young workers. Young workers of legal working age have, until the age of 18, the right to be protected from any type of employment or work which, by its nature or the circumstances in which it is carried out, is likely to jeopardise their health, safety or morals. Landscapers INC therefore requires all its suppliers to ensure that young workers are treated according to the law; this includes measures to avoid hazardous jobs, night shifts and ensure minimum wages. Limits for working hours and overtime should be set with special consideration to the workers’ young age.</p>
<h3>RESPONSIBILITIES</h3>
<p>Compliance, monitoring and review</p>
<p>All suppliers are obliged to keep Landscapers INC informed at all times about all places of production (including their sub-contractors). Any undisclosed production centres found would constitute a violation of this code of conduct.</p>
<p>Through the General Purchasing Conditions for the supply of products to Landscapers INC, Landscapers INC has reserved the right to make unannounced visits at any time to all places of production (including their sub-contractors) for goods intended for supply to Landscapers INC. Landscapers INC furthermore reserves the right to assign, at its sole discretion, an independent third party to conduct inspections in order to ensure compliance with Landscapers INC Child Labour policy.</p>
<p>Reporting No additional reporting is required.</p>
<p>Records management Staff must maintain all records relevant to administering this policy in a recognised Landscapers INC recordkeeping system RELATED LEGISLATION AND DOCUMENTS Labour Relations Act</p>
<h3>FEEDBACK</h3>
<p>The Child Labour Policy will be periodically reviewed to ensure continued relevance and adequacy. The Child Labour Policy shall be made available to all stakeholders on request. The SHERQ Management System will form an integral part of the company’s core business processes.</p>
<p>The responsibility of management and all employees to implement this policy effectively Ranks equally with their respective responsibilities for services, maintenance, quality, sales, costs, profitability, and similar matters of vital importance to the success of the company.</p>
<h3>APPROVAL</h3>
<p>CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.NAIDOO 02 January 2026</p>
<p>Child Labour Policy POL 008 Version: 00 Effective Date: 0 2-01-2026 Next Revision Date: 02-01-2027</p>', 'Child Labour Policy PURPOSE Landscapers INC Child Labour Policy has been established in order to make Landscapers INC position clear to suppliers and their co-workers, as well as any other parties. The requirements in this policy are mandatory to all suppliers and their sub-contractors. SCOPE Landscapers INC acknowledges the fact that child labour occurs in many countries. However, Landscapers INC does not accept child labour, and works actively against it. The complexity of the child labour issue requires a consistent, long-term effort to create sustainable and broad- based solutions in order to reach our goal; that no products delivered to Landscapers INC are produced by child labour. Landscapers INC respects different cultures and values in countries where Landscapers INC operates and sources its products but does not compromise on the basic requirements regarding the Rights of the Child. POLICY STATEMENT Landscapers INC may not require or permit a child to work if the child is under 15 years of age or is under the minimum school leaving age in terms of the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997. Landscapers INC may also not require or permit a child to perform such work or services that are inappropriate for his/her age; that places a risk to the child’s well-being, education, physical or mental health or social development. Implementation All actions to avoid child labour shall be implemented by taking the child’s best interests into account. Landscapers INC requires that all suppliers shall recognise the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997, chapter 6, “Prohibition of employment of children and forced labour”. This is regarded as a criminal offence as per the Basic Conditions of Employment Act 1997, Chapter 6. Suppliers are obliged to take the appropriate measures to ensure that no child labour occurs at suppliers’ and their sub-contractor’s places of production. If child labour is found in any place of production Landscapers INC will require the supplier to implement a corrective action plan. If corrective action is not implemented within the agreed time-frame, or if repeated violations occur Landscapers INC will terminate all business with the supplier concerned. The corrective action plan shall take the child’s best interests into consideration, i.e. family and social situation and level of education. Care shall be taken not merely to move child labour from one supplier’s workplace to another, but to enable more viable and sustainable alternatives for the child’s development. The supplier shall effectively communicate to all its sub-contractors, as well as to its own co- workers, the content of Landscapers INC Child Labour Policy, and ensure that all measures required are implemented accordingly. Young Workers Landscapers INC supports the legal employment of young workers. Young workers of legal working age have, until the age of 18, the right to be protected from any type of employment or work which, by its nature or the circumstances in which it is carried out, is likely to jeopardise their health, safety or morals. Landscapers INC therefore requires all its suppliers to ensure that young workers are treated according to the law; this includes measures to avoid hazardous jobs, night shifts and ensure minimum wages. Limits for working hours and overtime should be set with special consideration to the workers’ young age. RESPONSIBILITIES Compliance, monitoring and review All suppliers are obliged to keep Landscapers INC informed at all times about all places of production (including their sub-contractors). Any undisclosed production centres found would constitute a violation of this code of conduct. Through the General Purchasing Conditions for the supply of products to Landscapers INC, Landscapers INC has reserved the right to make unannounced visits at any time to all places of production (including their sub-contractors) for goods intended for supply to Landscapers INC. Landscapers INC furthermore reserves the right to assign, at its sole discretion, an independent third party to conduct inspections in order to ensure compliance with Landscapers INC Child Labour policy. Reporting No additional reporting is required. Records management Staff must maintain all records relevant to administering this policy in a recognised Landscapers INC recordkeeping system RELATED LEGISLATION AND DOCUMENTS Labour Relations Act FEEDBACK The Child Labour Policy will be periodically reviewed to ensure continued relevance and adequacy. The Child Labour Policy shall be made available to all stakeholders on request. The SHERQ Management System will form an integral part of the company’s core business processes. The responsibility of management and all employees to implement this policy effectively Ranks equally with their respective responsibilities for services, maintenance, quality, sales, costs, profitability, and similar matters of vital importance to the success of the company. APPROVAL CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.NAIDOO 02 January 2026 Child Labour Policy POL 008 Version: 00 Effective Date: 0 2-01-2026 Next Revision Date: 02-01-2027', true, 'manager', 'POL 008', '00', null, '2027-01-02', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/8.Child Labour Policy.pdf', true, '{}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, category = excluded.category, content = excluded.content, text = excluded.text, locked = excluded.locked, owner_role = excluded.owner_role, doc_code = excluded.doc_code, revision = excluded.revision, effective_date = excluded.effective_date, review_date = excluded.review_date, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, data = excluded.data where public.docs._seed and public.docs.updated_by is not distinct from public.docs.created_by;
insert into public.docs (id, title, category, content, text, locked, owner_role, doc_code, revision, effective_date, review_date, _src, _seed, data) values ('doc-policy-9-bb8ff6', 'Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure', 'policy', '<p>Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure</p>
<h3>PURPOSE</h3>
<p>This policy provides a framework for all Landscapers INC current and future sustainability activities.</p>
<h3>SCOPE</h3>
<p>This policy applies to all divisions, businesses, and staff (both permanent and contract), and to management and brand operations, where Landscapers INC is the controlling shareholder. Sustainability is a central function, which coordinates all sustainability activities in the divisions via the designated divisional champions and sustainability steering committee members.</p>
<h3>POLICY STATEMENT</h3>
<p>Sustainability is an approach to business that places value creation in a long-term context. Implicit in this statement is the creation of shared value. This implies that economic value is created for the business whilst simultaneously creating value for society, which enables the needs and challenges of society to be addressed. Business success should be linked to socio- economic development and low environmental impact. Sustainability is an approach to business that takes all three elements, economic, social and environmental value, into account. Landscapers INC is fully committed to good sustainability principles. We strive to be financially sound, socially responsible as well as environmentally friendly, with good corporate governance as the overarching principle.</p>
<p>Principles Governance</p>
<ul><li>Sustainability is an integral part of how Landscapers INC does business, and these principles are a core management principle;</li><li>Landscapers INC will comply with all relevant legislation and approved codes of good practice locally, nationally, and internationally;</li><li>Landscapers INC will communicate and report on progress, both internally and externally, principally, but not exclusively, by means of the annual integrated report;</li><li>Landscapers INC will utilise all suitable opportunities to influence our partners, suppliers, and contractors to improve their own sustainability performance;</li><li>Landscapers INC will constantly seek to improve environmental, governance, societal and economic performance on an ongoing basis;</li><li>Landscapers INC will participate in discussions about sustainable development matters; and</li><li>Landscapers INC will consider and implement initiatives to manage new and changing sustainability issues such as climate change, supply chain management, bribery and corruption, human rights, and crime.</li></ul>
<p>Social</p>
<ul><li>Landscapers INC will operate in a socially and ethically responsible manner;</li><li>Landscapers INC will raise awareness amongst its staff of our sustainability objectives;</li><li>Landscapers INC will encourage staff participation in sustainable development issues;</li></ul>
<p>Environmental</p>
<ul><li>Landscapers INC will minimise the consumption of energy and water resources and reduce waste production.</li><li>Landscapers INC will endeavour to reduce its carbon emissions in line with national target.</li></ul>
<h3>RESPONSIBILITIES</h3>
<p>Compliance, monitoring, and review The CEO will approve all policies and strategies regarding sustainability; The Management Representative will report to the CEO on sustainability Escalation of non-sustainable matters identified All non-sustainable practices that are identified will be escalated to the executive risk committee for consideration.</p>
<p>Records management Management must maintain all records relevant to administering this policy.</p>
<h3>RELATED LEGISLATION AND DOCUMENTS</h3>
<p>Occupational Health &amp; Safety Act (85 OF 1993) National Environmental Management Act 107 0f 1998 (NEMA)</p>
<h3>FEEDBACK</h3>
<p>The Sustainability policy will be periodically reviewed to ensure continued relevance and adequacy. The Sustainability Policy shall be made available to all stakeholders on request. The SHERQ Management System will form an integral part of the company’s core business processes. The responsibility of management and all employees to implement this policy effectively ranks equally with their respective responsibilities for services, maintenance, quality, sales, costs, profitability, and similar matters of vital importance to the success of the company.</p>
<h3>APPROVAL</h3>
<p>CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.NAIDOO 02 January 2026</p>
<p>Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure Effective Date: 02-01-2026 POL 009 Next Revision Date: 02-01-2027 Version: 00</p>', 'Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure PURPOSE This policy provides a framework for all Landscapers INC current and future sustainability activities. SCOPE This policy applies to all divisions, businesses, and staff (both permanent and contract), and to management and brand operations, where Landscapers INC is the controlling shareholder. Sustainability is a central function, which coordinates all sustainability activities in the divisions via the designated divisional champions and sustainability steering committee members. POLICY STATEMENT Sustainability is an approach to business that places value creation in a long-term context. Implicit in this statement is the creation of shared value. This implies that economic value is created for the business whilst simultaneously creating value for society, which enables the needs and challenges of society to be addressed. Business success should be linked to socio- economic development and low environmental impact. Sustainability is an approach to business that takes all three elements, economic, social and environmental value, into account. Landscapers INC is fully committed to good sustainability principles. We strive to be financially sound, socially responsible as well as environmentally friendly, with good corporate governance as the overarching principle. Principles Governance Sustainability is an integral part of how Landscapers INC does business, and these principles are a core management principle; Landscapers INC will comply with all relevant legislation and approved codes of good practice locally, nationally, and internationally; Landscapers INC will communicate and report on progress, both internally and externally, principally, but not exclusively, by means of the annual integrated report; Landscapers INC will utilise all suitable opportunities to influence our partners, suppliers, and contractors to improve their own sustainability performance; Landscapers INC will constantly seek to improve environmental, governance, societal and economic performance on an ongoing basis; Landscapers INC will participate in discussions about sustainable development matters; and Landscapers INC will consider and implement initiatives to manage new and changing sustainability issues such as climate change, supply chain management, bribery and corruption, human rights, and crime. Social Landscapers INC will operate in a socially and ethically responsible manner; Landscapers INC will raise awareness amongst its staff of our sustainability objectives; Landscapers INC will encourage staff participation in sustainable development issues; Environmental Landscapers INC will minimise the consumption of energy and water resources and reduce waste production. Landscapers INC will endeavour to reduce its carbon emissions in line with national target. RESPONSIBILITIES Compliance, monitoring, and review The CEO will approve all policies and strategies regarding sustainability; The Management Representative will report to the CEO on sustainability Escalation of non-sustainable matters identified All non-sustainable practices that are identified will be escalated to the executive risk committee for consideration. Records management Management must maintain all records relevant to administering this policy. RELATED LEGISLATION AND DOCUMENTS Occupational Health & Safety Act (85 OF 1993) National Environmental Management Act 107 0f 1998 (NEMA) FEEDBACK The Sustainability policy will be periodically reviewed to ensure continued relevance and adequacy. The Sustainability Policy shall be made available to all stakeholders on request. The SHERQ Management System will form an integral part of the company’s core business processes. The responsibility of management and all employees to implement this policy effectively ranks equally with their respective responsibilities for services, maintenance, quality, sales, costs, profitability, and similar matters of vital importance to the success of the company. APPROVAL CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.NAIDOO 02 January 2026 Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure Effective Date: 02-01-2026 POL 009 Next Revision Date: 02-01-2027 Version: 00', true, 'manager', 'POL 009', '00', '2026-01-02', '2027-01-02', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/9.Sustainability and Energy Efficiency Policy and Procedure.pdf', true, '{}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, category = excluded.category, content = excluded.content, text = excluded.text, locked = excluded.locked, owner_role = excluded.owner_role, doc_code = excluded.doc_code, revision = excluded.revision, effective_date = excluded.effective_date, review_date = excluded.review_date, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, data = excluded.data where public.docs._seed and public.docs.updated_by is not distinct from public.docs.created_by;
insert into public.docs (id, title, category, doc_code, content, text, locked, owner_role, _src, _seed, data) values ('doc-ppe-matrix', 'Matrix of Personal Protective Equipment (OHASA Regulation 2 - Personal Safety Equipment and Facilities)', 'policy', 'LI-FORM-001 page 2', '<p>Environments: General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Cold Storage Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</p><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Required in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cap</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Chemical Suit</td><td>Chemical Products</td></tr><tr><td>Conti Suit (2 piece)</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Cold Storage Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Dust Mask</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Earplugs #1</td><td> (Environmental Survey to be carried out to determine where applicable (issued per noise survey result, not by fixed environment; see Regulation 7 Noise and Hearing Conservation).)</td></tr><tr><td>Face Shield</td><td>Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Fur lined Leather Gloves</td><td>Cold Storage Operation</td></tr><tr><td>Gloves</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Goggles *</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Cold Storage Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop (Employees requiring spectacles/goggles to be fitted with prescription lenses.)</td></tr><tr><td>Gum Boots</td><td> (Not a legal requirement - HSE Committee might introduce for comfort.)</td></tr><tr><td>Hard Hat</td><td> (Hazardous Task ID to be carried out to determine where applicable.)</td></tr><tr><td>High Visibility Vest</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Jacket</td><td>Cold Storage Operation</td></tr><tr><td>Kidney Belt</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Stevedoring Operation, Transport Operation</td></tr><tr><td>Leather Gloves</td><td>Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Nylon Freezer Suit</td><td>Cold Storage Operation</td></tr><tr><td>PVC Rain Suit</td><td> (Not a legal requirement - SHE Committee might introduce for comfort.)</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory Mask</td><td>Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot</td></tr><tr><td>Rubber Gloves</td><td>Chemical Products</td></tr><tr><td>Safety Boots</td><td>General Cargo, Metal Products, Chemical Products, Washbay, Container Depot, Stevedoring Operation, Cold Storage Operation, Transport Operation, Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Sleeves</td><td>Workshop</td></tr><tr><td>Spectacles *</td><td> (Employees requiring spectacles/goggles to be fitted with prescription lenses.)</td></tr><tr><td>Visor</td><td>Transport Operation</td></tr><tr><td>Welding Shield</td><td>Workshop</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>This is a generic OHASA template without a landscaping column — see Data health.</em></p>', 'Cap Chemical Suit Conti Suit (2 piece) Dust Mask Earplugs #1 Face Shield Fur lined Leather Gloves Gloves Goggles * Gum Boots Hard Hat High Visibility Vest Jacket Kidney Belt Leather Gloves Nylon Freezer Suit PVC Rain Suit Respiratory Mask Rubber Gloves Safety Boots Sleeves Spectacles * Visor Welding Shield', true, 'manager', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Forms/PPE ISSUE FORM.pdf | page 2', true, '{}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, category = excluded.category, doc_code = excluded.doc_code, content = excluded.content, text = excluded.text, locked = excluded.locked, owner_role = excluded.owner_role, _src = excluded.