ers; sets culture and standards. | Coaches managers, holds staff accountable and solves issues before escalation. Owns expansion and final decision-making. | Implements systems, reports weekly, and turns priorities into action. </TABLE> Management Rhythm The GM should maintain a regular leadership rhythm that keeps the business aligned and makes accountability visible. Daily: Brief communication with managers on priorities, risks and urgent decisions. Weekly: Structured review of operations, sales, staff, customer issues and priorities with the CEO. Monthly: Identify the principal bottleneck, review performance trends, and propose improvements or training. Concluding Expectations Success in this role means the GM increasingly becomes the first point of leadership for the team. The business should not depend on the CEO to chase routine updates, solve every daily problem or direct individual staff members. The GM is expected to lead with ownership, keep the CEO informed through clear reporting, develop capable managers, and ensure that work is completed consistently through the company''s people and systems. General Manager Role & Responsibilities (images embedded: 0)', true, 'manager', 'x/General Manager-20260923T091726Z-1-001/General Manager/GM Responsibilities.docx', true, '{}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, category = excluded.category, content = excluded.content, text = excluded.text, locked = excluded.locked, owner_role = excluded.owner_role, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, data = excluded.data where public.docs._seed and public.docs.updated_by is not distinct from public.docs.created_by;
