insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-0aef44fe92ff3094cadeffa7', 'Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx', 'drive-management', 'fld-drive-management-general-manager-46be8c', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document', 14007, 'vault', 'Original company document · 2 records in the system came from it.', '["strategy roles"]'::jsonb, 'Leadership Development Programme General Manager Strategic Development Plan Strategic Intent This document outlines a comprehensive framework designed to cultivate executive-level leadership capabilities and operational excellence. The objective of this programme is to transition management personnel into proficient, professional leaders capable of autonomous business oversight while upholding the core values and institutional standards of Landscapers Inc. Programme Overview Name: Anthony Guruvadu Current Role: General Manager Business Unit: Landscapers Inc. Programme Duration: 12 Months Review Cycle: Weekly coaching sessions supplemented by quarterly performance evaluations. Commencement Date: 01 August 2026 Completion Date: 01 July 2027 Executive Leadership Philosophy A General Manager’s efficacy is determined not by individual effort, but by organizational outcomes. Leadership success is appraised based on: The performance and development of the team. Client satisfaction and relationship longevity. The sustained profitability of the business unit. The integrity and quality of executive leadership. Strategic problem-solving and decision-making capabilities. Baseline Executive Assessment Strengths Organizational loyalty and commitment. High standards of integrity and transparency. Proactive ownership of responsibilities. Exceptional professional work ethic. Operational, hands-on management approach. Competent administrative oversight. Fundamental financial literacy. Aptitude for continuous professional development. Development Areas Leadership presence Communication skills Approachability Daily planning and organisation Client relationship management Professional presentation Team accountability Time management Development Roadmap Quarter 1 – Build Structure Objectives Create and follow a daily schedule. Conduct daily morning team briefings. Improve communication with staff. Maintain professional appearance every day. Begin weekly CEO coaching meetings. Success Measures Daily planner completed. Team briefings held consistently. Weekly priorities achieved. Improved staff communication. Professional standard maintained. Quarter 2 – Lead People Objectives Delegates work effectively. Hold staff accountable. Conduct one-on-one conversations with employees. Resolve conflict professionally. Build confidence when leading the team. Success Measures Less CEO involvement in staff issues. Improved staff discipline. Clear delegation. Better morale. Quarter 3 – Build Client Relationships Objectives Visit key clients regularly. Handle complaints independently. Improve communication with customers. Identify opportunities for additional work. Success Measures Positive client feedback. Higher client retention. Increased upselling. Reduced customer complaints. Programme Success Criteria Objectives Understand monthly financial reports. Improve profitability. Identify cost savings. Present monthly business review to the CEO. Operate independently. Success Measures Monthly reporting completed. Improved margins. Independent decision-making. CEO involvement reduced. Weekly Coaching Meeting (45 Minutes- 1 hour) 1. Wins What went well this week? 2. Challenges What was difficult? 3. KPIs Revenue Jobs completed Staff attendance Customer issues Quotes outstanding Safety incidents 4. Leadership Development What leadership skill was practised this week? 5. CEO Feedback One thing done well. One thing to improve. 6. Next Week Three priorities. Leadership Competency Scorecard <TABLE> Competency | Current | Target | Q1 | Q2 | Q3 | Q4 Leadership Presence | 2.5 | 5.0 | | | | Communication Skills | 2.0 | 4.0 | | | | Planning & Organisation | 1.0 | 4.0 | | | | Client Relationships | 2.0 | 4.0 | | | | Financial Understanding | 3.0 | 4.0 | | | | Administration | 4.0 | 4.0 | | | | Professional Presentation | 2.0 | 5.0 | | | | Problem Solving | 3.0 | 4.0 | | | | Accountability | 2.0 | 4.0 | | | | </TABLE> Executive Commitments As CEO, I commit to: Coach rather than criticise. Give honest, timely feedback. Provide opportunities to lead. Hold consistent weekly meetings. Set clear expectations. Recognise progress and celebrate wins. Develop leaders, not followers. Candidate Commitments As General Manager, I commit to: Be coachable. Lead by example. Continue learning. Be organised. Communicate openly. Take ownership of results. Represent the business professionally. Definition of Success By the end of this programme, the General Manager should be capable of: Leading the team confidently. Managing operations and sales department effectively. Building strong client relationships. Running weekly meetings. Managing staff performance. Understanding business financials. Making sound operational decisions. Representing landscapers inc with professionalism and integrity. The ultimate goal is to create a leader who strengthens the business every day. (images embedded: 0)', 'x/General Manager-20260923T091726Z-1-001/General Manager/Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx', '[{"collection":"docs","id":"doc-strategy-leadership-development-programm-d5d0bc"},{"collection":"forms","id":"form-checklist-leadership-development-program-a99e99"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/General Manager-20260923T091726Z-1-001/General Manager/Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx', true, 'MANAGEMENT/General Manager/Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx', 'drive-management/file-0aef44fe92ff3094cadeffa7/Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx', '{"sha256":"0aef44fe92ff3094cadeffa7e0ab2c9e0077aa45f59761d2d21458acdee27be9","also_at":["x/General Manager-20260923T091726Z-1-001/General Manager/Landscapers inc Leadership Development Programme Anthony.docx"]}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = excluded.text_index, source_path = excluded.source_path, linked = excluded.linked, version = excluded.version, expires_on = excluded.expires_on, confidential = excluded.confidential, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-0b116f2d5a3ceadf5f8e5e8a', 'SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx', 'drive-management', 'fld-drive-management-sales-portfolio-c27689', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document', 11212, 'vault', 'Original company document · 2 records in the system came from it.', '["strategy roles"]'::jsonb, 'Landscapers Inc. Sales Workflow Purpose The purpose of this workflow is to ensure every sales enquiry is managed consistently, professionally, and efficiently from initial enquiry through to project handover. Every lead must follow the same process to ensure no opportunities are missed and every client receives excellent service. Sales Workflow Step 1 – Receive the Enquiry Enquiries may be received via: Phone call Email Website WhatsApp Referral Walk-in Social media Responsibility Salesperson Action Respond professionally. Gather the client’s information. Understand the service required. Step 2 – Record the Lead The salesperson must immediately record the enquiry in the Sales Pipeline. Information captured includes: Lead ID Date Company Contact Person Telephone Number Email Address Service Required Lead Source Assigned Salesperson Current Stage Current Stage New Lead Contacted Site Visit Booked Quote Sent Negotiating Won Lost Step 3 – Qualify the Lead Determine: Client requirements Property location Decision maker Budget (where appropriate) Whether a site visit is required Update the Sales Pipeline accordingly. Step 4 – Conduct the Site Visit Where required: Visit the site. Assess the scope of work. Take measurements. Take photographs. Discuss the client’s expectations. Record any special requirements. Step 5 – Prepare the Quotation Prepare an accurate quotation using the approved company quotation template. Ensure: Pricing is correct. Scope is clearly defined. Validity period is included. Terms and conditions are attached. Step 6 – Update the Quote Register Every quotation issued must be recorded. Capture: Quote Number Client Date Issued Quote Value Status Expiry Date Step 7 – Send the Quote Send the quotation promptly. Confirm that the client has received it. Step 8 – Follow Up The salesperson is responsible for following up all outstanding quotations. Possible outcomes include: Awaiting decision Negotiating Additional information requested Won Lost The Sales Pipeline and Quote Register must always reflect the latest status. Step 9 – Quote Accepted Once accepted: Update the Sales Pipeline to Won. Update the Quote Register to Won. Create the client in the CRM (Client Register). The CRM must include: Company Name Contact Person Telephone Number Email Address Site Address Services Provided Contract/Retainer Value Notes Step 10 – Create the Client Folder Create a client folder containing: Signed quotation Contract Site photographs Plans (if applicable) Supporting documents Client correspondence Step 11 – Handover to Operations Provide Operations with: Client details Signed quotation Scope of work Site information Photos Special instructions Required start date Operations now assumes responsibility for delivering the project. Step 12 – Finance Finance is responsible for: Raising invoices Recording payments Updating the accounting system Following up outstanding debtors where necessary Step 13 – Management Reporting The General Manager reviews sales performance weekly. Key metrics include: New Leads Quotes Issued Quote Value Quotes Won Quotes Lost Conversion Rate Revenue Won Outstanding Quotes Salesperson Performance The CEO reviews these reports with the General Manager during management meetings to monitor performance and support business growth. Workflow Summary Enquiry Received ↓ Sales Pipeline ↓ Qualify Lead ↓ Site Visit ↓ Prepare Quote ↓ Quote Register ↓ Send Quote ↓ Follow Up ↓ Won ↓ CRM (Client Register) ↓ Create Client Folder ↓ Handover to Operations ↓ Operations Delivers ↓ Finance Invoices ↓ Management Reporting (images embedded: 0)', 'x/SALES PORTFOLIO-20260923T091822Z-1-001/SALES PORTFOLIO/SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx', '[{"collection":"docs","id":"doc-strategy-sales-workflow-sales-process-so-45b045"},{"collection":"forms","id":"form-checklist-sales-workflow-sales-process-s-cd51d3"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/SALES PORTFOLIO-20260923T091822Z-1-001/SALES PORTFOLIO/SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx', true, 'MANAGEMENT/SALES PORTFOLIO/SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx', 'drive-management/file-0b116f2d5a3ceadf5f8e5e8a/SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx', '{"sha256":"0b116f2d5a3ceadf5f8e5e8a2b05c8cc5f720f1727dbf54ddcd13f6206db6a3f","also_at":["x/SALES PORTFOLIO-20260923T091822Z-1-001/SALES PORTFOLIO/SALES PROCESS SOP OVERVIEW.docx"]}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = excluded.text_index, source_path = excluded.source_path, linked = excluded.linked, version = excluded.version, expires_on = excluded.expires_on, confidential = excluded.confidential, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-0b6574a3d30b24753b433821', 'Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx', 'drive-sops', 'fld-drive-sops-sops-50b84f', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document', 11366, 'vault', 'Original company document · 1 record in the system came from it.', '["sops toolbox"]'::jsonb, 'Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) 1. Purpose The purpose of this SOP is to establish a consistent process for executing all jobs safely, efficiently, and professionally. It ensures every job is completed to the company’s quality standards while delivering an excellent customer experience. 2. Scope This SOP applies to all operational employees, supervisors, and managers involved in delivering services from the time the team arrives on site until the job is completed and closed. 3. Responsibilities General Manager Monitor overall operational performance. Resolve operational issues beyond the authority of the Operations Manager. Review job performance and identify opportunities for improvement. Operations Manager Ensure all jobs are properly prepared before departure. Allocate teams, vehicles, equipment, and materials. Monitor job progress. Support operational staff where required. Ensure company procedures are followed. Team Supervisor Lead the team on site. Conduct the pre-job briefing. Ensure safety requirements are followed. Monitor workmanship throughout the job. Communicate with the client when required. Complete the final quality inspection. Operational Employees Perform work according to company standards. Follow all safety procedures. Wear required PPE. Use company equipment responsibly. Report hazards, incidents, and equipment faults immediately. Represent the company professionally. 4. Procedure Step 1 – Arrival on Site Upon arrival, the Team Supervisor must: Park vehicles safely. Introduce the team to the client where appropriate. Confirm the work to be completed. Identify any site-specific hazards. Ensure the work area is safe before commencing. Step 2 – Team Briefing Before work begins, the Team Supervisor must brief the team on: Scope of work. Individual responsibilities. Safety requirements. Client expectations. Special instructions. Estimated completion time. Step 3 – Equipment and Safety Checks Before commencing work: Inspect all equipment. Confirm PPE is being worn correctly. Ensure all required materials are available. Remove any faulty equipment from service. Verify vehicles and equipment are positioned safely. Step 4 – Execute the Work The operational team must: Complete the work according to company standards. Follow approved work methods. Protect the client’s property. Maintain a clean and organised work area. Work efficiently without compromising quality or safety. Immediately report any unexpected issues. Step 5 – Client Communication During the job: Keep the client informed of progress where appropriate. Communicate any delays or unforeseen issues. Obtain approval before performing additional work outside the agreed scope. Maintain a professional and courteous attitude at all times. Step 6 – Monitor Quality Throughout the job, the Team Supervisor must: Inspect completed sections of work. Correct defects immediately. Ensure work continues to meet company standards. Provide guidance to team members where required. Step 7 – Site Clean-Up Once the work is complete: Remove all waste and debris. Clean the work area. Return equipment to the vehicle. Ensure no company tools or materials remain on site. Leave the client’s property in a clean and professional condition. Step 8 – Final Quality Inspection Before leaving site, the Team Supervisor must confirm: All agreed work has been completed. Company quality standards have been met. The site is clean and safe. Equipment has been packed away. Any outstanding issues have been resolved or communicated. Step 9 – Job Completion Before departing: Thank the client where applicable. Obtain client sign-off if required. Record any additional work completed. Report damaged equipment or incidents. Notify the Operations Manager that the job has been completed. Step 10 – Update Operational Records Following completion of the job: Update the Job Register. Complete the Quality Control Checklist. Record maintenance requirements if identified. Submit job photos where applicable. Notify Administration that the job is ready for invoicing. 5. Records The following documents must be updated where applicable: Job Register Daily Schedule Quality Control Checklist Equipment Register Vehicle Register Maintenance Register Incident Register 6. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) The Operations Team should aim to achieve: Jobs completed safely. Jobs completed on schedule. High-quality workmanship. Minimal rework. High client satisfaction. Zero preventable incidents. Professional client interactions. Proper care of company assets. 7. Review This SOP will be reviewed periodically to ensure operational efficiency, consistent service delivery, and continuous improvement as the business grows. (images embedded: 0)', 'x/SOPS-20260923T091755Z-1-001/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx', '[{"collection":"docs","id":"doc-sop-job-execution-sop-60a8b2"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/SOPS-20260923T091755Z-1-001/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx', true, 'SOP''S & TEMPLATES/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx', 'drive-sops/file-0b6574a3d30b24753b433821/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx', '{"sha256":"0b6574a3d30b24753b43382155e94db401ccc00d26351fa338d8a887ead7c134","also_at":["x/SOPS-20260923T091755Z-1-001/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx","x/SOPS-20260923T091755Z-1-001/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx","x/SOPS-20260923T091755Z-1-001/SOPS/Job Execution Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).docx"]}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = excluded.text_index, source_path = excluded.source_path, linked = excluded.linked, version = excluded.version, expires_on = excluded.expires_on, confidential = excluded.confidential, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
