insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-3bc2f414763e37fafcb8ab6f', 'Management  Contract.pdf', 'drive-legal', 'fld-drive-legal-company-documents-e43812', 'application/pdf', 4055959, 'vault', 'Original company document · 1 record in the system came from it.', '["company compliance"]'::jsonb, 'LANDSCAPERS INC Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management SITE MANAGEMENT EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT Professional Employment Agreement Prepared for: LANDSCAPERS INC 🌿 Excellence in Landscaping & Property Management 🌿 CONFIDENTIAL DOCUMENT LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 2 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. SITE MANAGER Employment Agreement 🌿 1. PARTIES This Employment Agreement is entered into between: EMPLOYER DETAILS Employer Name: Registration Number: Address: EMPLOYEE DETAILS Employee Name: ID Number: Residential Address: Collectively referred to as "the Parties". 🌿 2. APPOINTMENT The Employer hereby appoints the Employee as Site Manager commencing on: Start Date: The Employee accepts the appointment and agrees to perform all duties associated with the position. 🌿 3. PLACE OF WORK LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 3 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. Primary Place of Work: The Employee may be required to travel and work at various project sites as directed by the Employer. 🌿 4. PROBATION PERIOD The Employee shall be subject to a probation period of three (3) months commencing from the Start Date. During probation, performance, conduct, attendance, and suitability for the position shall be assessed. 🌿 5. JOB DESCRIPTION & DUTIES The Employee shall perform the duties of Site Manager, including but not limited to: ✦ Supervising site staff and subcontractors ✦ Managing daily site operations ✦ Ensuring compliance with health and safety regulations ✦ Monitoring project progress and quality standards ✦ Managing materials, equipment, and site resources ✦ Reporting project status to management ✦ Conducting site inspections ✦ Ensuring client satisfaction and professional service delivery ✦ Maintaining company records and documentation ✦ Any other reasonable duties related to the position 🌿 6. WORKING HOURS Monday to Friday: Hours: The Employee may be required to work reasonable additional hours to meet operational requirements. Where the Employee qualifies as a senior managerial employee, the provisions regulating ordinary hours and overtime may not apply. 🌿 7. REMUNERATION LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 4 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. Monthly Salary (R): Payment Date (day of month): Payable monthly into the Employee''s nominated bank account. Statutory deductions including PAYE, UIF and any other lawful deductions shall be made. 🌿 8. BENEFITS The Employee shall be entitled to: ✦ UIF contributions as prescribed by law ✦ Annual leave ✦ Sick leave ✦ Family responsibility leave ✦ Public holiday benefits ✦ Any additional benefits offered by the Employer 🌿 9. ANNUAL LEAVE The Employee shall be entitled to twenty-one (21) consecutive days annual leave per leave cycle or the equivalent as prescribed by law. Leave must be approved in advance by management. 🌿 10. SICK LEAVE The Employee shall be entitled to sick leave in accordance with the Basic Conditions of Employment Act (BCEA). Medical certificates may be required where applicable. 🌿 11. FAMILY RESPONSIBILITY LEAVE The Employee shall be entitled to family responsibility leave as prescribed by legislation. LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 5 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. 🌿 12. HEALTH AND SAFETY The Employee shall: ✦ Comply with all Occupational Health and Safety requirements ✦ Wear prescribed Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) when required ✦ Report hazards, incidents, and injuries immediately ✦ Participate in safety training and toolbox talks Failure to comply with safety requirements may result in disciplinary action. 🌿 13. COMPANY PROPERTY All company property, including but not limited to the following, shall remain the property of the Employer and must be returned upon termination of employment: ✦ Vehicles ✦ Equipment and tools ✦ Laptops and mobile phones ✦ Documents and records 🌿 14. CONFIDENTIALITY The Employee shall not disclose any confidential information relating to the following, both during and after employment: ✦ Clients and client relationships ✦ Pricing and contract details ✦ Financial information and trade secrets ✦ Business operations and strategic plans 🌿 15. DISCIPLINARY CODE The Employee agrees to comply with all company rules, policies, procedures, and disciplinary codes. Misconduct may result in disciplinary action up to and including dismissal in accordance with South African labour legislation. LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 6 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. 🌿 16. TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT Either party may terminate this agreement by providing written notice as follows: ✦ One (1) week — if employed for less than six (6) months ✦ Two (2) weeks — if employed for more than six months but less than one year ✦ Four (4) weeks — if employed for one year or longer Or as otherwise required by applicable law. 🌿 17. RESTRAINT OF TRADE (OPTIONAL) For a period of ______ months after termination, the Employee shall not directly solicit the Employer''s existing clients for competing services within a radius of ______ kilometres. This clause shall only apply to the extent that it is lawful and enforceable under South African law. 🌿 18. ENTIRE AGREEMENT This agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior discussions and understandings. Any amendment must be made in writing and signed by both Parties. 🌿 19. GOVERNING LAW This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa. SIGNATURES By signing below, both parties agree to the terms and conditions of this employment contract. EMPLOYER EMPLOYEE LANDSCAPERS INC | Site Management Employment Contract Page 7 of 7 LANDSCAPERS INC | Property Maintenance • Landscaping • Site Management CONFIDENTIAL: This document is intended solely for the named parties. Unauthorised disclosure is prohibited. Name: Position: Signature: Date: Name: Signature: Date: 🌿 LANDSCAPERS INC | Excellence in Every Project 🌿', 'x/Company Documents-20260923T091637Z-1-001/Company Documents/Management  Contract.pdf', '[{"collection":"compliance_docs","id":"cd-tpl-tpl-site-mgr-f14be6"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/Company Documents-20260923T091637Z-1-001/Company Documents/Management  Contract.pdf', true, 'LEGAL AND COMPLIANCE/Company Documents/Management  Contract.pdf', 'drive-legal/file-3bc2f414763e37fafcb8ab6f/Management  Contract.pdf', '{"sha256":"3bc2f414763e37fafcb8ab6f19b943fbfde544191d4ca8ee339fc0eca6e6dfd4"}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = exclude