insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-699ccfa866b9bece764f439e', '5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf', 'drive-sops', 'fld-drive-sops-h-s-policies-3157d8', 'application/pdf', 157057, 'vault', 'Original company document · 1 record in the system came from it.', '["hs policies procedures"]'::jsonb, 'Business Ethics and Performance Policy PURPOSE In line with the Landscapers INC Quality Policy and organizational goal of excellence, it is vital for Landscapers INC and its employees to abide by a strict ethical code. Since the integrity of its employees underlies Landscapers INC relationship with Customers, clients and communities, the highest standards of ethical business Conduct are required by employees in fulfilling their company responsibility. SCOPE This policy applies to and is binding upon all Landscapers INC employees, including supplementary Labour, contractors, and consultants. This policy incorporates the principles enshrined in the South African Constitution, as well as relevant statutes, corporate governance practices, and Landscapers INC Policies and Procedures. POLICY STATEMENT Ethics are an attitude towards doing business in the best possible way. Ethics include such things as living Landscapers INC values, sound corporate Governance, respect for diversity and Human rights, and acting with Integrity. Ethics involve a clear, conscious commitment to do the right thing at all times. PRINCIPLES Ethics is an attitude towards doing business in the best possible way. It does not simply mean doing what is legal in any situation; it also means doing what is ethically right. Landscapers INC Ethical Values are as follows: - • Respect, dignity, and equal opportunity. • Employee development. • Participation and empowerment. • Providing a safe and healthy environment. • Accepting accountability for actions and decisions. • Treating everyone fairly, consistently, sensitively, honestly and with respect for individual rights. • Acting with honesty, openness, and integrity in all dealings with colleagues, company, customers, and other stakeholders. • Complying with the law as well as Landscapers INC policies, codes of conduct and procedures. • Landscapers INC supports employees in their quest to abide by strict ethical Guidelines. PERFORMANCE To enable Landscapers INC to deliver Customer Satisfaction, increased productivity is essential. The productivity can only be increased via training of employees to be efficient in all core activities that are critical for the success, profitability, and sustainability of this business, therefore these learning processes are to enhance the employee’s performance. The Training and Development Programs are as follows ▪ Competency based Training and Development. ▪ Competency based Performance Management. ▪ Competency based Recruitment and Selection. ▪ Competency based Assessment. Landscapers INC strives to be recognized as an equal opportunity employer, for this reason the following assessment criteria are used: • Assessment of learning Potential • Assessment of Management Potential • Career Development Assessment • Assessment of suitability of students for various courses of study Business Ethics and Performance Policy POL 005 Version: 00 Effective Date: 02-01-2026 Next Revision Date: 02-01-2027 These training and development programs will enable this organization to Co-ordinate individual activities to deliver Customer satisfaction efficiently and effectively. This will also enhance the reflexive competence in demonstrating the ability to reflect on, evaluate, adapt and improve in a variety of contexts. STRATEGIC OBJECTIVES Landscapers INC mission is to increase its market share in the Landscaping Sector therefore the strategic objective of Landscapers INC is to develop an integrated Education, Training and Human Resources Development Plan to unlock the full potential of all human resources within Landscapers INC, this will add value to the social and economic sustainability of the organization. This strategic objective will be achieved through the development of employee’s competence levels as well as increased levels of return on costs and investment in education and training. It is encouraged to adopt a culture of life-long learning skills by creating: • A workplace, which is an active learning environment • Opportunities to acquire new skills These learning interventions are to minimize or eliminate costly mistakes, which derive from incompetence and enhance cost efficiency and cost effectiveness. Together we begin a pilgrimage aimed at ensuring that we really achieve organizational excellence. It is a fact that without rules our lives would be chaotic. Imagine what driving would be like if there were no rules of the road to guide and assist us. Similarly, policies and procedures are intended to assist us in the performance of our work Although all employees are expected to comply with these policies and procedures, they are also expected to interpret them reasonably in order for them to achieve the full effect. Whilst Management will keep these policies and procedures under constant review, employees who feel they should be amended are requested to present the matter to the relevant manager, who will then make the necessary amendments if so required. RESPONSIBILITIES Compliance, monitoring and review All employees have a responsibility to act in accordance with the ethical obligations and principles outlined in this policy. Compliance is a condition of employment. Managers must ensure that this policy and its guidelines are strongly and clearly communicated to all employees. It is Management’s endeavor to develop Human Resources by ensuring that employees acquire all necessary skills in cargo handling in accordance with Skills Development act, Sector Skills plan, and Workplace Skills plan. Reporting No additional reporting is required. Records management Staff must maintain all records relevant to administering this policy in a recognised recordkeeping system APPROVAL CEO Initial and Surname Signature Date J.E.NAIDOO 02 January 2026', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf', '[{"collection":"docs","id":"doc-policy-5-33f27b"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf', true, 'SOP''S & TEMPLATES/H&S/Policies/5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf', 'drive-sops/file-699ccfa866b9bece764f439e/5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf', '{"sha256":"699ccfa866b9bece764f439ea57bf8bdb341c804017102815cf5897d48bb3247","also_at":["x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/5.Business Ethics and Performance Policy.pdf"]}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = excluded.text_index, source_path = excluded.source_path, linked = excluded.linked, version = excluded.version, expires_on = excluded.expires_on, confidential = excluded.confidential, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
