cluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
insert into public.files (id, name, drive_id, folder_id, mime, size, kind, description, tags, text_index, source_path, linked, version, expires_on, confidential, _src, _seed, vault_path, storage_path, data) values ('file-b1a084ae01cb81db2305c8c9', '13.HIV Policy.pdf', 'drive-sops', 'fld-drive-sops-h-s-policies-3157d8', 'application/pdf', 185323, 'vault', 'Original company document · 1 record in the system came from it.', '["hs policies procedures"]'::jsonb, 'HIV Policy PURPOSE This policy aims to develop a sense of responsibility within the Role players of Landscapers INC - being the Employers, Employees and Unions, the families and communities in which employees live. SCOPE The Role players will strive to address the economic and social conditions under which the employees live, which may increase the risk of HIV infection. In all matters relating to HIV/AIDS the Role players will deal fairly and justly with employees who are living with this epidemic, in accordance with constitutional, regulatory and employment equity principles. The AIDS programme is a joint responsibility of the Role players (Employers, Employees and Unions), who must UNITE their efforts to deal with this responsibly. POLICY STATEMENT UNDERLYING PRINCIPLES This HIV/AIDS policy is based on the recognition of six principles underlying this document. The Role players must be able to cope with the additional burden likely to be placed on it by HIV/AIDS and the steps taken to contain it. The Role players will endeavour to manage this epidemic and reduce the effect on and consequences of HIV/AIDS for the Role player The Role players will endeavour to promote understanding of and lifelong learning about the HIV/AIDS epidemic. All Role players commit to this policy, its implementation and sustainability. In all dealings regarding HIV/AIDS, the Role players will aim to balance the needs of people with HIV/AIDS against other employees as well as those of the employer. The particular role of STDs in the HIV epidemic shall be recognized by the Role players. The Role players will endeavour to provide all employees with access to STD counselling and treatment and to educate them about the links between STDs and HIV. If the Role players cannot provide STD services directly, they will attempt to assist employees to obtain such services in the community (e.g. by referral of employees to the local Clinic.) DEALING WITH HIV/AIDS IN THE WORKPLACE NON-DISCRIMINATION • The Role players will not unfairly discriminate against any employees, or applicants for jobs, on the basis of their actual or suspended HIV status, or that of their relatives. Any employees with HIV/AIDS will receive the same consideration in the working environment while symptom free, as any other able-bodied employee. Once the person becomes HIV-ill, the employee will receive the same consideration as any employee with any other illness or incapacity. • The Role players commit themselves to dealing with employees with HIV/AIDS in the same way as they deal with all other employees. Unfair discrimination, insensitivity, or rejection of employee’s known to have HIV/AIDS will not be tolerated. Disciplinary action will be taken against those who breach these Policy Guidelines. • Employees with HIV /AIDS will be afforded the usual opportunities for career development, such as training, conference attendance as well as promotion opportunities • There will be no unfair discrimination towards employees with HIV or unfair withholding of such opportunities. • An employee with HIV/AIDS is expected to meet the same performance requirements that apply to other employees, with reasonable, negotiated accommodation, as described in the Labour Relations Act, regarding incapacity. HIV Policy POL 013 Version: 00 Effective Date: Next Revision Date: 02-01-2026 02-01-2027 HIV TESTING/ SCREENING OF EMPLOYEES AND PROSPECTIVE CANDIDATES • In line with the principle of non-discrimination, employees and applicants for employment will NOT be required: • To have an HIV test, whether this is for employment, promotion or merit assessment. • To disclose their own HIV status, or any member of the family’s HIV status. Further, standard medical tests will not include HIV testing. • When an employee is too ill to continue working, he/she can be medically boarded after consultation with relevant human resources and medical personnel. This is done in terms of standard boarding procedures. • All employees may be required to undergo periodic or regular medical check-ups by the employer or by Law, where this relates to an inherent requirement of the job. However, such tests exclude HIV testing. BENEFITS • Employees with HIV/AIDS will be eligible for all the standard employee benefits. • An HIV test shall not be required for admission to any sector-controlled benefit scheme. However, certain non-sector benefit schemes may require pre-benefit HIV testing, resulting in limitations, exclusions or premium loading. In this case, the Role players will inform employees accordingly. • The employer shall endeavour to use agencies that offer the most favourable benefits, and that are, as far as possible, viable and non-discriminatory, balancing the interests of all parties. CONFIDENTIALITY This right to privacy is a basic human right and also applicable to the employment situation. The following broad guidelines should assist the Role players in dealing with sensitive matters, and specifically with HIV/AIDS, STDs, and other personal or health issues. • The road freight sector is committed to a workplace in which rights and obligations are recognized and where confidentiality and privacy are maintained. • An employee who is aware that he/she has HIV/AIDS is not required to disclose his/her HIV/AIDS diagnosis to anyone in the work place or to any Role players at any stage. • The employee may only be required to furnish the employer with a report on the fitness of the employee to do his/her normal job (i.e. Medical personnel can only report on the employee’s fitness to work, and not the actual diagnosis). • All personal details of all employees, including the actual or suspected HIV status of any employee, shall be strictly confidential. • Any information about an employee’s HIV status shall be revealed only with their express written consent, after counselling regarding the rights of and consequences for the employee. • If an employee with HIV/AIDS decides to disclose his/her diagnosis to a colleague, supervisor or manager, that person should take all reasonable measures to ensure that this information remains private and confidential. • The Role players will not tolerate any breaches of confidentiality. Any employee who breaches such confidentiality shall be subject to appropriate disciplinary measures, which could include dismissal. REFUSAL TO WORK WITH EMPLOYEES HIV/AIDS • No employee shall be entitled to refuse to work with an employee with HIV/AIDS. Any prejudice or discrimination will be dealt with through established disciplinary procedures. • In the event of an employee/s, refusing to work with someone who is suspected to be, or is known to have HIV/AIDS, suitable persons within the Role players (or consultants) will counsel that employee/s. HIV Policy POL 013 Version: 00 Effective Date: Next Revision Date: 02-01-2026 02-01-2027 • If after such efforts the employee/s still refuses to work alongside someone who has HIV/AIDS, then appropriate disciplinary action may be taken against the employee/s. COUNSELING AND SUPPORT OF EMPLOYEES WITH HIV/AIDS • The employer will endeavour to provide all employees with HIV/AIDS with access to suitable counselling. This may be done either through the employer, or via referral to suitable community- based services. • Where possible, this counselling will also be available for employees whose partners may have HIV/AIDS, or who may have other infected family members. • The Role players will endeavour to assist employees needing hospital, hospice or other such facilities. To this end, the Role players may contribute donations to such facilities with a view to making them more accessible to employees and their families. • There are certain measures, which may extend the life span of a person with HIV (e.g. good health care and nutrition). To this end, the Role players will endeavour to provide employees with HIV/AIDS with nutritional supplements (e.g. vitamins) and prophylactic medication where this is', 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/13.HIV Policy.pdf', '[{"collection":"docs","id":"doc-policy-13-a10cae"}]'::jsonb, 1, null, false, 'x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/13.HIV Policy.pdf', true, 'SOP''S & TEMPLATES/H&S/Policies/13.HIV Policy.pdf', 'drive-sops/file-b1a084ae01cb81db2305c8c9/13.HIV Policy.pdf', '{"sha256":"b1a084ae01cb81db2305c8c955df256135e8bd68eabe1fc80edf435e56cc3433","also_at":["x/H&S-20260923T091746Z-1-001/H&S/Policies/13.HIV Policy.pdf"]}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do update set name = excluded.name, drive_id = excluded.drive_id, folder_id = excluded.folder_id, mime = excluded.mime, size = excluded.size, kind = excluded.kind, description = excluded.description, tags = excluded.tags, text_index = excluded.text_index, source_path = excluded.source_path, linked = excluded.linked, version = excluded.version, expires_on = excluded.expires_on, confidential = excluded.confidential, _src = excluded._src, _seed = excluded._seed, vault_path = excluded.vault_path, storage_path = excluded.storage_path, data = excluded.data where public.files._seed and public.files.updated_by is not distinct from public.files.created_by;
